From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <jameswdumay@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skippy): passthrough empty SET destinations in stage replay

A 0-token ubatch (the state-handoff flush pass) rebuilds SET destinations
empty. Chameleon's image-logit suppression splice is the only recorded SET
producer and its constant-size img_logits source asserts against the empty
destination in ggml_set_impl, aborting the handoff. Pass the empty
destination through unchanged: the recorded set is vacuous there, and every
other family replays zero SET operations.
---
diff --git a/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp b/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
index e7b4d212a..c134ae58d 100644
--- a/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
+++ b/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
@@ -609,6 +609,14 @@ ggml_tensor * replay_operation(
             tensor = ggml_cumsum(context, sources[0]);
             break;
         case GGML_OP_SET:
+            // A 0-token ubatch rebuilds the destination empty and the recorded set
+            // is vacuous there; passthrough keeps the empty output instead of
+            // tripping ggml_set_impl's element-count assert (chameleon's
+            // constant-size image-logit splice is the only SET producer).
+            if (ggml_nelements(sources[0]) == 0) {
+                tensor = sources[0];
+                break;
+            }
             tensor = operation.alias_source == 0
                     ? ggml_set_inplace(context, sources[0], sources[1],
                             operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 0), operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 1),
